const relTol = 2e-4

// normTol is the bound for everything after the tail's channel norm, and it
// is measured, not chosen (all numbers 2026-09-20). The pre-norm stages run
// at magnitudes ~1e4, where an fp32 summation-order difference is a real
// absolute quantity; the per-pixel L2 norm then rescales the tensor to O(1)
// and small elements' inherited drift surfaces as elementwise rel ~5e-3.
// The reference does the same to itself: against a float64 decode, the
// dumped fp32 run is rel 1.3e-3 at norm_out (3.4e-4 at the image), and
// changing only its thread count moves it 8.6e-4. On the *image*, this
// port's distance from the dump is max abs 8.7e-4 in [-1, 1] — under a
// quarter of one 8-bit quantization step. A structural mistake shows here
// at rel ≥ 1e-1, so the loosened bound still catches every modeled error.
const normTol = 8e-3

